    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0394" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg306"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Herbert.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Unofficial.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-02"><hi rendition="#italic">September 2,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Herbert</hi>: In further response to your
                    unofficial note of the 26th ultimo, I regret that I am unable to procure the
                    detailed information you desire in regard to the traffic passing through the
                    Sault Ste. Marie Canal, as I am informed by the Treasury Bureau of Statistics
                    that the data prepared and furnished to that office are not capable of being
                    classified under the headings you indicate, month by month.</p>
                <p>The inclosed proof sheets from a report now in the hands of the printer, and
                    probably to be issued in about a fortnight, contains all the information the
                    Bureau of Statistics can now give me concerning the traffic in question.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
